###############################################################################
# Q10 -- Benchmark results (Q11 inference-cost properties inline)
###############################################################################

# No energy/force/stress accuracy metric is reported in a form the schema captures (see Q12).

###############################################################################
# Q11 -- Computational resources
###############################################################################

# Throughput on one NVIDIA RTX PRO 6000 (80 GB) for amorphous SiO2 (Fig.
# 11): SevenNet-Omni 3.695 ns/day (70 atoms) to 0.093 ns/day (15,120 atoms,
# out of memory beyond), SevenNet-0 6.356 to 0.104 ns/day (70 to 70,000
# atoms), MACE-mp-0-small 4.703 to 0.166 ns/day, SevenNet-Nano-6.0 9.895 to
# 0.170 ns/day; per-atom times are 86,400 s / (ns/day x 1e6) / atoms. The
# distilled models train for two epochs; training times are not given.

###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - Validation MAEs on the teacher-labelled data are stated only as ranges over the four cutoffs (23-27 meV/atom, 0.078-0.083 eV/A, 4.52-4.82 kbar), and benchmark results (Matbench, defects, molecules, MOFs, adsorption, diffusivity, densities) are figure-only or in Supplementary Tables; none is encoded.
# - The solvent fine-tuning of SevenNet-Nano-5.0 (1,203 configurations of DFEC, cis-DFEC and trans-DFEC) and the SiO2 etching fine-tuning are not encoded as separate runs. Authors are taken from the front matter (the manifest row has no DOI).
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: paper front matter).
# - Evaluation roles and data, base models, inference timings with their system sizes, and the source location of each value are recorded in the encoding input (artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/oh2026.yaml) until the schema has terms for them.
